  {
    "sha": "752eb5a774b06cfc62b0b97ffdd2352e17312c53",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDc1MmViNWE3NzRiMDZjZmM2MmIwYjk3ZmZkZDIzNTJlMTczMTJjNTM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-09T03:52:49Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-09T03:52:49Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(setup): each op on its own setup's mount; one NC file per mount\n\nEvery law that judges an existing operation now reads that operation's\nown setup's machine and post instead of the active setup's: generation\n(machine kind, spindle housing, rotaries), the lathe spindle law and its\nstamp clause, the rest reading's lathe rule, the aligned-setup gate, the\nmill-only stock carry (both ends), the fixture table (table_box per\nsetup), the gate's spindle-housing walk, the limit check (one check per\nmachine over the ops its setups run) and the retype/paste family gate.\nThe ribbon, the Setup pane and the new-op door keep the active mount.\n\nThe #343 one-mount refusals are retired: an inactive setup's op\ngenerates on its own machine without activation, and a program whose\nsetups span machines or posts posts one file per mount\n(posting::post_mounts, <stem>_<nn>_<setups>.<ext>), each byte-identical\nto posting that setup alone. Per-op files post each op through its own\nsetup's post and machine. The UI Post command, cam.post, MCP post and\nCLI process -o follow; a one-mount program is one file, unchanged.\n\nFixes #388\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
